  "body": "Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).\n\nDepends on: #541.\n\nDerive an electrode solid from selected cavity faces, offset by undersize and orbit, and extended to a pickup/holder stub. Degenerate or self-intersecting results are a clean error by name, never a panic.\n\n**Done means:** a pocket's faces yield an electrode that burns that pocket in the sim, and degenerate face sets are refused. Fuzz-style degenerate input tests included.",
